## Why This Is Asked

Tests ability to design a scheduler that balances SLA guarantees with cost efficiency in a multi-tenant, cross-region LLM-ops environment.

## Key Concepts

- Quality of Service with per-tenant quotas and budgets
- Preemption mechanisms and priority queue management
- Cost modeling and real-time optimization dashboards
- Regional routing strategies and data locality considerations

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudocode: token-bucket burst control
function canSubmit(tenant) {
  const bucket = tenants[tenant];
  if (bucket.tokens > 0) {
    bucket.tokens--;
    return true;
  }
  return false;
}
```

## Why This Is Asked

Tests ability to implement cost-aware, latency-conscious routing in a simple, auditable way. Focuses on per-tenant accounting, model pricing, and practical test coverage.

## Key Concepts

- Cost-aware routing and SLA mapping
- Per-tenant ledger and budget enforcement
- Simple fallback behaviors and test plans

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo: ledger update and routing decision
function routePrompt(tenant, prompt) {
  const remaining = tenant.budget - tenant.spent;
  for (const m of ['fast','balanced','accurate']) {
    if (cost(m, prompt) <= remaining && latency(m, prompt) <= tenant.sla[m]) {
      tenant.spent += cost(m, prompt);
      return m;
    }
  }
  return 'cached';
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you extend this to handle budget rollovers and monthly resets?
- How would you test this with A/B experiments across tenants?

## Why This Is Asked

This tests practical rate limiting, tenant isolation, and testability in an LLM gateway.

## Key Concepts

- Per-tenant quotas and burst caps
- Token bucket and optional leaky bucket hybrids
- Isolation in Redis or in-memory stores

## Code Example

```javascript
class TokenBucket {
  constructor(capacity, refillPerSec) {
    this.capacity = capacity;
    this.refillPerSec = refillPerSec;
    this.tokens = capacity;
    this.lastRefill = Date.now();
  }
  allow(n = 1) {
    const now = Date.now();
    const elapsed = (now - this.lastRefill) / 1000;
    this.tokens = Math.min(this.capacity, this.tokens + elapsed * this.refillPerSec);
    this.lastRefill = now;
    if (this.tokens >= n) { this.tokens -= n; return true; }
    return false;
  }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you monitor per-tenant leakage and detect abuse?
- How would you scale buckets across multiple gateway instances?

